  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a severe upward bias when historical volatility is high and recent sentiment scores are low (0.00-0.20), failing to account for mean reversion risks.",
    "Forecasts systematically overshoot true outcomes by 5-10% during periods of rising sentiment, ignoring the lag effect where price spikes precede sustained growth.",
    "When historical data shows a downward trend followed by low sentiment, the model incorrectly projects a linear recovery rather than a volatile bounce-back.",
    "The model fails to capture 'V-shaped' recoveries in the first 10 days of the forecast horizon, assuming gradual drift instead of sharp reversals.",
    "High volatility environments (standard deviation > 3) require a downward correction factor of 8-12% on the initial forecast to align with true outcomes."
  ]
